From 08a4471560422f597e62b40c083e7c0ec68f0e22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zac <zac@zacbowling.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Jan 2026 15:15:32 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 26/27] wifi: mt76: mt7925: fix race condition in async ROC
 abort

Remove the clear_bit(MT76_STATE_ROC) call from mt7925_roc_abort_async()
to fix a race condition where mac80211 might not receive the ROC expiry
notification.

The race sequence was:
  1. roc_work runs and checks abort flag - NOT set yet
  2. mt7925_roc_abort_async sets abort flag
  3. mt7925_roc_abort_async clears ROC flag
  4. roc_work checks ROC flag - CLEARED! Returns without cleanup
  5. ieee80211_remain_on_channel_expired never called

By leaving the ROC flag set, roc_work will properly handle either case:
  - If it sees abort flag: handles abort path (clears both flags)
  - If it sees ROC flag: handles normal expiry path

Either way, mac80211 receives proper notification.

Reported-by: Cursor Bot (code review)
Signed-off-by: Zac Bowling <zac@zacbowling.com>
---
 .../net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7925/main.c   | 18 ++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7925/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7925/main.c
index b6f9ec1458..7dce8c0fa0 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7925/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7925/main.c
@@ -453,12 +453,22 @@ static void mt7925_roc_abort_async(struct mt792x_dev *dev)
 {
 	struct mt792x_phy *phy = &dev->phy;
 
-	/* Set abort flag first - roc_work checks this before acquiring mutex */
+	/* Set abort flag - roc_work checks this before acquiring mutex.
+	 *
+	 * IMPORTANT: Do NOT clear MT76_STATE_ROC here. There's a race:
+	 *   1. roc_work checks abort flag - not set yet
+	 *   2. We set abort flag here
+	 *   3. If we cleared ROC flag here...
+	 *   4. roc_work checks ROC flag - cleared! Returns without cleanup
+	 *   5. mac80211 never gets ieee80211_remain_on_channel_expired
+	 *
+	 * By leaving ROC flag set, roc_work will either:
+	 *   - See abort flag set: handle abort path (clears both flags)
+	 *   - See ROC flag set: handle normal expiry (clears ROC flag)
+	 * Either way, mac80211 gets properly notified.
+	 */
 	set_bit(MT76_STATE_ROC_ABORT, &phy->mt76->state);
 
-	/* Clear ROC state */
-	clear_bit(MT76_STATE_ROC, &phy->mt76->state);
-
 	/* Stop the timer - use non-sync version to avoid blocking */
 	timer_delete(&phy->roc_timer);
 
